#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
DRM v0.3 (repair pass) — Displacement-Replacement Model
=======================================================

Standalone numerical research tool. Python 3.8+, stdlib only.

REPAIR PASS NOTES
-----------------
This file is the repair-pass build. It is delivered under a new
filename so the original is not overwritten. On first start it
creates one-time .pre_repair.bak copies of the data files that
already exist. Existing archive records are read as-is and are
NOT reinterpreted under the new event-annotation policy.

CORE EPISTEMIC RULES (unchanged)
--------------------------------
* T0 features use only information available at the observation.
* T1+ outcomes are measured separately using later observations.
* Live snapshots have no future outcome attached.
* Similarity, frequencies, and measurements are descriptive only.

REPAIR DELTAS
-------------
FIX-1  Menu option X runs the full historical research pass.
FIX-2  Per-marker event annotation mode; only contemporaneous
       knowledge enters T0 DNA. Legacy integer markers are read
       as mode "unknown" and are excluded from T0 DNA.
FIX-3  Instrument-aware pip size (JPY vs non-JPY). Unknown
       instruments do not inherit a guessed value. FX pairs only;
       metals, crypto, indices return None.
FIX-4  Starting price (single- and multi-candle) is stored
       separately from the reference anchor. Retracements to
       anchor and to starting price are reported distinctly and
       as signed progress toward the reference.
FIX-5  Multi-candle cumulative displacement and duration are
       descriptive fields only (no DNA or fingerprint change).
FIX-6  return_mad_rw window slice corrected.
FIX-7  Same-dataset distinct episodes may match; a module-level
       MAX_MATCH_DISTANCE rejects weak matches.
FIX-8  Optional timestamps; ordering/duplicate validation;
       explicit oldest-to-newest confirmation when absent.
FIX-9  Z and E displayed with precise, model-specific meaning.

Live-quote anomaly warning (display only): a provisional
percentage threshold produces a visible warning when the live
quote differs unusually from the last completed close. The
quote is not rejected and neither value is inferred wrong.

MENU
----
B — Batch inject historical prices
E — Annotate historical event positions (per-marker mode)
R — Historical reconstruction at a selected observation
L — Live reconstruction from a manually entered MT5 quote
X — Run full historical research pass (build/update archive)
H — Historical episode archive
S — Archive summary
D — Dataset status
C — Configuration and DNA registry
Q — Quit
"""

